[I] Utilities for fast date-time calculations and conversion

[T] Dateutils are a bunch of command-line tools for working with dates and
[T] times, with a focus on use cases arising from large amounts of financial
[T] data. The commands, like dadd, ddiff, dseq, dconv, dgrep, dround and
[T] dtest, resemble known Unix tools and calculate, convert, filter and
[T] generate dates in many formats.

[U] https://www.fresse.org/dateutils/

[A] Dateutils Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 0.4.11
